exam: It is given that trees are to be planted along one side of a road of {L} m in length at intervals of {d} m, a tree being placed at each extremity. Determine the total number of trees to be planted.
exam: Whereas lamp posts are erected at intervals of {d} m along a path of {L} m, inclusive of one post at either end, ascertain the number of lamp posts so erected.
exam: Ascertain the number of posts required for a straight fence of {L} m, the posts being set {d} m apart and one post being set at each end.
exam: Flags are positioned at regular intervals of {d} m along a straight running track of {L} m, commencing at the start and terminating at the finish. State the number of flags so positioned.
exercise: Along the {L} m path to Grandad's final resting place, a rose bush stands every {d} m, with one at each end. How many rose bushes are there?
exercise: The old poplars along the {L} m lane all gave up the ghost, so new ones go in every {d} m, with one at each end. How many new trees are planted?
